 publication-type="book"><name><surname>Hartenberger</surname><given-names>J-L</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Luckett WP, Hartenberger J-L</person-group><article-title>The order Rodentia: Major questions on their evolutionary origin, relationships and suprafamily systematics</article-title><source>Evolutionary Relationships Among Rodents: a Multidisciplinary Analysis</source><year>1985</year><publisher-name>New York: Plenum Press</publisher-name><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>33</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Hartenberger</surname><given-names>J-L</given-names></name><article-title>Description de la radiation des Rodentia (Mammalia) du Pal&#x000e9;oc&#x000e8;ne sup&#x000e9;rieur au Mioc&#x000e8;ne; incidences phylog&#x000e9;n&#x000e9;tiques</article-title><source>C R Acad Sci Paris</source><year>1998</year><volume>326</volume><fpage>439</fpage><lpage>444</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B9"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Landry</surname><given-names>SO</given-names></name><article-title>A proposal for a new classification and nomenclature for the Glires (Lagomorpha and Rodentia)</article-title><source>Mitt Mus Nat Berl Zool Reihe</source><year>1999</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>283</fpage><lpage>316</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B10"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Huchon</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Catzeflis</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name><name><surname>Douzery</surname><given-names>JPE</given-names></name><article-title>Variance of molecular datings, evolution of rodents and the phylogenetic affinities between Ctenodactylidae and Hystricognathi</article-title><source>Proc R Soc London ser B</source><year>2000</year><volume>267</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>402</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1098/rspb.2000.1014</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B11"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Farwick</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Jordan</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Fuellen</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Huchon</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Catzeflis</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Brosius</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><article-title>Automated scanning for phylogenetically informative transposed elements in Rodents</article-title><source>Syst Biol</source><year>2006</year><volume>55</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>936</fpage><lpage>948</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/10635150601064806</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17345675</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B12"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Marivaux</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Vianey-Liaud</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jaeger</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><article-title>High-level phylogeny of early Tertiary rodents: dental evidence</article-title><source>Zool J Linn Soc</source><year>2004</year><volume>142</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>105</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1096-3642.2004.00131.x</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Waddell</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Shelley</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><article-title>Evaluating placental inter-ordinal phylogenies with novel sequences including RAG1, gamma-fibrinogen, ND6, and mt-tRNA, plus MCMC-driven nucleotide, amino acid, and codon models</article-title><source>Mol Phylogenet Evol</source><year>2003</year><volume>28</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>197</fpage><lpage>224</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1055-7903(03)00115-5</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12878459</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B14"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Lavocat</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Parent</surname><given-names>J-P</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Luckett WP, Hartenberger JL</person-group><article-title>Phylogenetic analysis of middle ear features in fossil and living rodents</article-title><source>Evolutionary Relationships Among Rodents: a Multidisciplinary Analysis</source><year>1985</year><publisher-name>New York: Plenum press</publisher-name><fpage>333</fpage><lpage>354</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B15"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Luckett</surname><given-names>WP</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Luckett WP, Hartenberger JL</person-group><article-title>Superordinal and intraordinal affinities of rodents:developemental evidence from the dentition and placentation</article-title><source>Evolutionary Relationships Among Rodents: a Multidisciplinary Analysis</source><year>1985</year><publisher-name>New York: Plenum press</publisher-name><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>278</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B16"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Vianey-Liaud</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Luckett WP, Hartenberger J-L</person-group><article-title>Possible evolutionary relationships among Eocene and lower Oligocene rodents in Asia, Europe and North America</article-title><source>Evolutionary Relationships Among Rodents: a Multidisciplinary Analysis</source><year>1985</year><publisher-name>New York: Plenum Press</publisher-name><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>309</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B17"><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><name><surname>Wahlert</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><person-group person-group-type="editor">Luckett WP, Hartenberger J-L</person-group><article-title>Cranial foramina of rodents</article-title><source>Evolutionary Relationships Among Rodents: a Multidisciplinary Analysis</source><year>1985</year><publisher-name>New York: Plenum Press</publisher-name><fpage>311</fpage><lpage>332</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B18"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Sarich</surname><given-names>VM</given-names></name><article-title>Of Molecules, Comparative Anatomy, and the Fossil Record &#x02013; the Evolutionary Messages Cannot Conflict</article-title><source>Am J Phys Anthropol</source><year>1985</year><volume>66</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>224</fpage><lpage>224</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B19"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Adkins</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Walton</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Honeycutt</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><article-title>Higher-level systematics of rodents and divergence time estimates based on two congruent nuclear genes</article-title><source>Mol Phylogenet Evol</source><year>2003</year><volume>26</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>409</fpage><lpage>420</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1055-7903(02)00304-4</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12644400</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B20"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Huchon</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Madsen</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Sibbald</surname><given-names>MJJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ament</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Stanhope</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Catzeflis</surname><given-names>FM</given-names></name><name><surname>De Jong</surname><given-names>WW</given-names></name><name><surname>Douzery</surname><given-names>JPE</given-names></name><article-title>Rodent phylogeny and a ti